},{"kind":"identifier","text":"Interaction_DragView"}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Reproduces the runner reference’s fixed layer hierarchy and framing: a full-screen"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"magenta canvas and a centered white card. The card maps "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"origami.Drag"},{"type":"text","text":" Position to"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"its offset. Release projects momentum, applies the Drag patch’s logical bounds, and"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"pulses Reset when both position axes are within the placed graph’s 100-point center"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"tolerance."}],"title":"Interaction_DragView","role":"symbol","kind":"symbol","type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/swami\/interaction_dragview"},"doc://samatwork.Swami/documentation/Swami/Interaction_DragView/accessibility(identifier:)":{"title":"accessibility(identifier:)","url":"\/documentation\/swami\/interaction_dragview\/accessibility(identifier:)","abstract":[],"identifier":"doc:\/\/samatwork.Swami\/documentation\/Swami\/Interaction_DragView\/accessibility(identifier:)","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"accessibility"},{"kind":"text","text":"("},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"identifier"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:SS","text":"String"},{"kind":"text","text":") -> "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:7SwiftUI15ModifiedContentV","text":"ModifiedContent"},{"kind":"text","text":"<"},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Self"},{"text":", ","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:7SwiftUI31AccessibilityAttachmentModifierV","text":"AccessibilityAttachmentModifier","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":">","kind":"text"}],"deprecated":true,"type":"topic","role":"symbol","kind":"symbol"},"doc://samatwork.Swami/documentation/Swami":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/samatwork.Swami\/documentation\/Swami","url":"\/documentation\/swami","role":"collection","type":"topic","title":"Swami","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"An Origami → SwiftUI translator: a deterministic parser reads Facebook’s "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".origami"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"patch graph into a semantic IR, and a codegen writes that IR out as SwiftUI. Swami"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"is also the patch-matched helper library that fills gaps between Origami patches"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"and native SwiftUI — one helper per Origami patch, named after the patch, sized by"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Origami’s patch surface. Every pattern that lands is a deliverable, verified against"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Origami’s own render, and shipped as a DocC-embedded example."}],"kind":"symbol"}}}